{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"clearRightSiblingID"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","title":"clearRightSiblingID()","externalID":"s:6Yorkie0A19_V1_TreeRestoreSpanV19clearRightSiblingIDyyF","modules":[{"name":"Yorkie"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"mutating"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"clearRightSiblingID"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan\/clearrightsiblingid()"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan\/clearRightSiblingID()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clears the value of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rightSiblingID"},{"type":"text","text":". Subsequent reads from it will return its default value."}],"references":{"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan":{"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"TreeRestoreSpan carries a tree node run from a single deletion, addressed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by TreeNodeID identity, for identity-preserving Tree undo\/redo. Unlike the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text RestoreSpan (flat offsets), a tree span records the node’s structure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(type\/attrs) and its position anchors, because in a tree id-order is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sibling-order: left_sibling_id and right_sibling_id are redundant external"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary anchors of the deleted run, so restore can reconstruct the run’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal order from the op’s own spans and needs only one surviving"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary to place it. value\/attributes are a deep copy so a GC-purged node"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be recreated."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie","title":"Yorkie","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie"},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan/clearRightSiblingID()":{"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan\/clearrightsiblingid()","kind":"symbol","title":"clearRightSiblingID()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clearRightSiblingID","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clears the value of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rightSiblingID"},{"type":"text","text":". Subsequent reads from it will return its default value."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan\/clearRightSiblingID()","role":"symbol"}}}